<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n13308" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dērīsus</span></b> ,
			ūs, m.
		derideo, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>mockery, scorn, derision</i> (perh. not ante-Aug.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">facile ad derisum stulta levitas ducitur,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Phaedr. 5, 7, 3</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Sen. Contr. 4</span></i> prooem.; <i><span class="en">Quint. 6, 3,
				7</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Tac. Agr. 39</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">esp.: in derisum facere,</span>”
				<i>to mock, put to scorn</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg. Jer. 20, 7 sq.</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">id. Thren. 3, 14</span></i>; cf.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">in derisum habere, dare,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. Sap.
					5, 3</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">12, 25</span></i>.</div>
